==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|orv|порожьнъ}}, from earlier {{l|orv|пороздьнъ}}, inherited from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*porzdьnъ}}. {{doublet|ru|пра́здный}}, a borrowing from Old Church Slavonic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|поро́жний}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Jordónus-порожний.wav|a=Moscow}}

===Adjective===
{{ru-adj|поро́жний}}

# [[empty]] {{gloss|devoid of content}}
#: {{syn|ru|пусто́й}}
#: {{syn|ru|порозжий}}
#: {{syn|ru|я́ловый}}

====Declension====
{{ru-decl-adj|поро́жний|a*}}
* Note: the form "поро́жен" is very rare

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ru|порожня́к|g=m}}
''Compound words:''
* {{l|ru|пустопоро́жний}}
''Compounds:''
